# Offline passages and vocabulary from the original Python seed banks.
# The vocabulary contains lexicon seed entries and words in the sentence seed.
include "./passages.elisa"

module PassageSeed:
    def passages() -> Passages::Bank:
        can Memory.Allocate, Abort.Panic:
            return Passages::read("The farmer got up before the sun. He fed the hens and milked the cow. Then he sat down to eat his breakfast.\nIt began to rain in the afternoon. The children ran inside to keep dry. They played cards until the sky cleared.\nA small bird built a nest in the old tree. She laid three blue eggs in it. A few weeks later the chicks hatched.\nThe baker mixes flour and water in a large bowl. He leaves the dough to rise for an hour. Then he shapes it and bakes it in the oven.\nWater boils when it gets hot enough. The steam rises from the pot. When the steam cools it turns back into water.\nThe library opens at nine in the morning. People come to read and to borrow books. It closes again at six in the evening.\nIce forms on the lake in the winter. When it is thick enough people skate on it. In the spring the ice melts and the boats come back.\nThe cat sat by the door all morning. She was waiting for her owner to come home. When the door opened she ran to meet him.\nPlants need light to grow. They use it to make food from water and air. Without light most plants turn yellow and die.\nThe train left the station on time. It stopped at four small towns on the way. Two hours later it reached the city.\nMy grandmother keeps a garden behind her house. She grows beans and tomatoes there. Every summer she gives the extra food to her neighbours.\nThe bridge was built over the river many years ago. At first only people on foot could use it. Later it was made wider for cars.\nA doctor listens to the heart of a patient. If the beat is strange she asks more questions. Sometimes she sends the patient for more tests.\nBees fly from flower to flower in the summer. They collect a sweet liquid called nectar. Back at the hive they turn it into honey.\nThe storm knocked down many trees in the night. In the morning the roads were closed. Workers spent the whole day clearing them.\nTom wanted to learn to play the piano. He practised for an hour every day. After a year he could play his favourite song.\nThe moon goes around the earth about once a month. It has no light of its own. We see it because it reflects the light of the sun.\nThe shop sells fresh fruit and bread. Most people buy their food there on the way home from work. On Sundays the shop is closed.\nA fire needs heat and fuel and air. If one of them is taken away the fire goes out. That is why water can stop a fire.\nThe children planted a tree at the school. They watered it every week. Ten years later it gave shade to the whole yard.\nOur team lost the first game of the season. The coach made us train harder. We won every game after that.\nFish breathe through gills on the sides of their heads. Water flows in through the mouth. The gills take the air out of the water.\nThe old man walked slowly up the hill. At the top he sat on a bench. From there he could see the whole town.\nSnow fell all night and covered the road. In the morning the bus could not get through. The school was closed for the day.\nThe museum has a large collection of old coins. Some of them are more than two thousand years old. Visitors can look at them through glass.\nA spider spins a web to catch insects. The threads are thin but very strong. When an insect gets stuck the spider wraps it in silk.\nShe opened the letter with shaking hands. It said that she had got the job. She called her mother to tell her the news.\nThe river flows down from the mountains. It passes through farms and small villages. At last it reaches the sea.", true)

    def sentences() -> Passages::Bank:
        can Memory.Allocate, Abort.Panic:
            return Passages::read("the black horse walked along the road\na cat and a dog sat under the tree\nthe river runs south through the green field\nshe read the book for three hours\nthe king had a long white beard\nwe found a small stone house near the wood\nthe child came home before the rain\nhis brother works in a shop on the street\nthe sun goes down behind the hill\nthey built a bridge over the water\na bird sang in the tree outside her window\nthe doctor said that he should rest\nthe wind was cold and the snow fell\nmy friend wrote a long letter to his family\nthe girl kept the key in her hand\nthe fire burned in the room until morning\nthe boat came into the town from the sea\neach part of the work took an hour\nthe paper on the table had his name on it\nthey walked through the garden to the door\nthe horse and the cow stood in the field\nthe young girl learned to read\na white bird flew over the water\nthe price of the land went up again\nhe took the money out of his pocket\nthe story of the town is very old\nthe sheep were kept behind a stone wall\nshe gave the letter to the man at the door\nthe tree by the river lost all its leaves\nthe school stands between the church and the market\nthe food was good and the room was warm\nhis voice was quiet but every word was clear\nthe road turns left before it reaches the sea\nthe little boy was afraid of the dark\nthey sat by the fire and told stories\nthe light of the moon fell across the floor\nthe woman put the bread on the table\na red flower grew between the grey stones\nthe men worked in the field until dark\nwe saw many people on the city street\nthe young man became a doctor\nthe wolf came down from the hills in winter\nshe held the small bird in both hands\nthe paper said that the war was over\nthe water in the river was cold and clear\nhe could not find the right word for it\nthe house had a red roof and a green door\nthe old book was full of pictures\nthey left the city early in the morning\nthe dog ran across the grass to the water\nher father was a farmer in the north\nthe sound of music came from the window\nthe wall of the church is made of stone\na long line of people stood outside the shop\nthe ice on the water was thick\nhe asked the same question three times\nthe leaves of the tree turned brown\nthe queen sat still and said nothing\nthe train left the station on time\na heavy rain fell on the town all night\nthe man carried the box up the stairs\nthe old woman gave her name to the young man\nthe boy put his hand on the cold glass\nthere was a light in the window of the house\nthe ship went down near the coast\nshe opened the door and looked outside\nthe horse would not cross the bridge\nthey gave the child a book about birds\nthe grass in the field was wet with rain\nhis father built the house with his hands", false)

